think Studied both parents -- image/click_side.rye (the per-query which-side read from the cross product's SIGN over doubled group-frame centers) and image/region_partition.rye (the whole-scene CONTAINED/CLIPPED/OUTSIDE partition, its classes pixel-exact from each object's own box). The crux writes itself as the EXACT INVERSION: region_partition classifies each object by its OWN box (a per-object geometric fact, pixel-exact), line_partition classifies each object by the center of the GROUP it belongs to (a connectivity fact), deliberately COARSER -- so a line NEVER splits a connected group.
think Confirmed the compose surface keyed by cluster id, not by tap: overlap_clusters.cluster_of maps object->group, cluster_facts.cluster_bbox reads a group's union frame (its doubled midpoint the group center), click_order.click_group_id + click_collinear.click_group_center_doubled resolve the two anchor taps. So the whole-scene partition classifies every object by label without re-tapping, and cross-checks the on-set against click_side.which_side with representative taps.
think Designed the scene: 7 objects on a 22x15 canvas -- U above (label 1), a STRADDLING connected group G = P1 corner-L box (16,1)-(18,3) + P2 corner-L box (18,3)-(20,13) whose boxes overlap only at P1's empty bottom-right corner (18,3) so they stay 8-disconnected components in ONE cluster (labels 2,3), anchors A box (2,5)-(3,6) and B box (10,5)-(11,6) (labels 4,5), N box (14,5)-(15,6) on the line (label 6), W box (6,9)-(7,10) below (label 7). The horizontal line A->B at doubled-y 11 partitions LEFT {U}, ON {A,B,N}, RIGHT {P1,P2,W}: P1's own box center (34,4) is LEFT and P2's (38,16) is RIGHT, yet both classify RIGHT (group center (36,14) below the line) -- the group never split.
